==English==

===Etymology===
From {{affix|en|en-|-crypt}}, from {{der|en|grc|κρυπτός||lit=hidden, concealed, private, secret}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ɪnˈkɹɪpt/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-encrypt.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɪpt|s=2}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# To [[conceal]] [[information]] by means of a [[code]] or [[cipher]].
#: {{syn|en|encode}}
#: {{ant|en|decode|decrypt}}
#: {{ux|en|All messages on this platform are doubly '''encrypted''' to increase security.}}
# {{lb|en|cryptography}} To [[transform]] [[information]] using [[encryption]] in a way that it is believed only authorized parties can [[decode]].
#: {{ux|en|The data was '''encrypted''' in transit using AES-GCM.}}

====Derived terms====
{{col|en|encryptable|encrypter|encryptor|reencrypt|signcrypt|superencrypt|unencrypt
|self-encrypting
}}

====Related terms====
