{{also|Emerald}}
==English==
[[Image:Beryl_emeralds_cut_XH.jpg|thumb|right|cut emeralds (beryl)]]
{{wp}}

===Etymology===
{{etymon|en|:inh|enm:emeraude|tree=1}}
From {{inh|en|enm|emeraude}}, borrowed from {{der|en|fro|esmeraude}}, from {{der|en|la-vul|*smaralda}}, {{m|la|*smaraldus}}, {{m|la|*smaraudus}}, variant of {{der|en|la|smaragdus}}, from {{der|en|grc|σμάραγδος}}, {{m|grc|μάραγδος}}, from a {{der|en|sem|-}} language. Compare {{cog|he|בָּרֶקֶת|tr=bāréqeṯ||emerald, flashing gem}}, {{cog|akk|𒁀𒊏𒄣|tr=baraqu|lit=scintillation}}, {{cog|ar|بَرْق|lit=flashing}}, {{cog|egy|bwyrqꜣ|lit=to sparkle}}:{{egy-h|D58-Z7-Z4:D21-N29-Z1-G1-D6}} and loanwords with Semitic etymon such as {{cog|sa|मरकत}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈɛm.(ə.)ɹəld/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-emerald.wav|a=Southern England}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{senseid|en|Q43513}}Any of various green [[gemstone]]s, especially a green [[transparent]] form of [[beryl]], highly valued as a precious stone.
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2012-03
|author=Lee A. Groat|title=Gemstones
|volume=100|issue=2|page=128
|magazine=w:American Scientist
|url=http://www.americanscientist.org/issues/feature/2012/2/gemstones
|passage=Although there are dozens of different types of gems, among the best known and most important are diamond, ruby and sapphire, '''emerald''' and other gem forms of the mineral beryl, chrysoberyl, tanzanite, tsavorite, topaz and jade.
|accessdate=17 May 2013|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20120614165157/http://www.americanscientist.org/issues/feature/2012/2/gemstones|archivedate=14 June 2012
}}
# [[emerald green|Emerald green]], a colour.
#: {{color panel|047853}}
# {{lb|en|tincture}} {{cap|vert}}, when [[blazon]]ing by precious stones.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1726|author=John Guillim|title=The Banner Display'd|page=504
|passage=16. As the first. ''Crest'', on a Mount '''Emerald''', a Falcon rising Topaz.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1754|author=John Lodge|title=The Peerage of Ireland; Or, a Genealogical History of the ...|page=212
|passage=''Crest''. On a Wreath, a demi Dragon, '''Emerald''', armed and langued, Roby [...] ''Supporters''. Two Dragons reguardant, '''Emerald''', [...]}}
#* {{RQ:Melville Omoo
|passage=Some of the lagoons, said to have subterranean outlets, have no visible ones; the inclosing island, in such cases, being a complete zone of '''emerald'''.}}
# Any [[hummingbird]] in the  [[genus|genera]] {{taxfmt|Chlorostilbon|genus}} and ''[[Elvira]]''; and some in the [[genus]] {{taxfmt|Amazilia|genus}}
# {{lb|en|entomology}} Any of various species of [[dragonfly]] of the family {{taxlink|Corduliidae|family}}.
# {{lb|en|dated|printing|UK}} A [[size]] of [[type]] between [[nonpareil]] and [[minion]], [[standardize]]d as 6½-[[point]].

