# In the reproductive cycle, the stage after the fertilization of the egg that precedes the development into a [[fetus]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2015-08-18|author=Clelia De-la-Peña; et al.|title=The role of chromatin modifications in somatic embryogenesis in plants|journal=Frontiers in Plant Science|url=http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC4539545/|doi=10.3389/fpls.2015.00635|volume=6|issue=|pages=
|passage=SE onset depends on a complex network of interactions among plant growth regulators, mainly auxins and cytokinins, during the proembryogenic early stages, and ethylene and gibberellic and abscisic acids later in the development of somatic '''embryos'''.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2015-12-04|author=|title=Divergent RNA Localisation Patterns of Maternal Genes Regulating Embryonic Patterning in the Butterfly Pararge aegeria|journal=PLOS ONE|url=http://journals.plos.org/plosone/article?id=10.1371/journal.pone.0144471|doi=10.1371/journal.pone.0144471|volume=|issue=|pages=
|passage=In situ hybridisations were performed on devitellinised '''embryos''' still wrapped around the yolk and on '''embryos''' with the yolk dissected away.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Susan Scutti|title=Climate change will affect gender ratio among newborns, scientists say|magazine=w:CNN|url=https://www.cnn.com/2019/01/23/health/climate-change-infant-sex-ratio-intl/index.html|date=2019-01-23|passage=Though scientists do not know how stress affects gestation, Fukuda theorizes that the vulnerability of Y-bearing sperm cells, male '''embryos''' and/or male fetuses to stress is why “subtle significant changes in sex ratios” occur.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20250916231045/https://www.cnn.com/2019/01/23/health/climate-change-infant-sex-ratio-intl/index.html|archivedate=16 September 2025}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Brenda Goodman|title=Scientists report creation of first human synthetic model embryos|magazine=w:CNN|url=https://www.cnn.com/2023/06/14/health/human-model-embryo/index.html|date=2023-06-14|passage=They include cells that would typically go on to develop a yolk sac, a placenta and the '''embryo''' itself.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20260605030039/https://www.cnn.com/2023/06/14/health/human-model-embryo/index.html|archivedate=5 June 2026}}
# An [[organism]] in the earlier stages of development before it emerges from the egg, or before [[metamorphosis]].
# In a [[viviparous]] [[animal]], the young animal's earliest stages in the mother's body.
# In a [[human]], usually the [[cell]] growth of the child within the mother's body, through the end of the seventh week of [[pregnancy]].
# {{lb|en|botany}} A [[rudimentary]] [[plant]] [[contained]] in the [[seed]].
# {{lb|en|figurative}} The [[beginning]]; the first stage of anything.
