====Usage notes====
Because the words ''elegy'' and {{m|en|eulogy}} sound and look similar and both concern speeches or poems associated with someone's death and funeral, they are easily confused. A simple key to remembering the difference is that an elegy is chiefly about {{l|en|lament#Verb|lamenting}} whereas a eulogy is chiefly about {{l|en|praise#Verb|praising}} (and {{m|en|eu-#English|eu-}} = "good").<!--Morehead et al 3e supports this summary.-->

