#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2013-06-14|author=[http://www.guardian.co.uk/profile/sam-leith Sam Leith]|volume=189|issue=1|page=37|magazine=w:The Guardian Weekly|title=[http://www.guardian.co.uk/books/2013/may/23/holy-shit-history-swearing-mohr Where the profound meets the profane]|passage=Swearing doesn't just mean what we now understand by "dirty words". It is '''entwined''', in social and linguistic history, with the other sort of swearing: vows and oaths.}}
